def append_pair(n,text):
 global s
 pat=r'(?=^### KT-%02d —)'%(n+1)
 if n==51: s=s.rstrip()+'\n\n'+text+'\n'; return
 m=re.search(pat,s,re.M)
 if not m: raise ValueError(n)
 s=s[:m.start()].rstrip()+'\n\n'+text+'\n\n'+s[m.start():]
append_pair(4,'**Additional owned framing contract:** `thm-seifert-zero-framing-and-framing-integer` proves a positive surface-normal push-off has linking zero, and relative framing classes of a fixed oriented knot form a Z-torsor via π1(SO(2)). A Seifert surface selects its zero. The framed diagram theorem follows by ordinary R moves with compensating integer twists, using the existing framed-tangle presentation; no unframed R1 is a framed identity.')
append_pair(8,'**Rack and fundamental-quandle closure:** `def-rack-fundamental-quandle-and-adjoint-group` defines a rack by bijective right translations and right self-distributivity, a quandle by adding a*a=a, the diagram-presented fundamental quandle with one generator per under-arc, and the adjoint group with relations e_(a*b)=e_b^(-1)e_a e_b. `thm-fundamental-quandle-and-adjoint-group-from-wirtinger` proves presentation independence by local quandle Tietze transformations and identifies the adjoint group of the knot presentation with the KT-01 Wirtinger group. It makes no completeness/classification claim. `thm-rack-colorings-are-framed-invariants` proves R2/R3 coloring bijections and tracks the kink map under framed R1 compensation; unframed R1 requires idempotency. `alg-finite-rack-quandle-coloring-from-table` takes a finite multiplication table, checks each axiom exhaustively, and enumerates all arc assignments or returns an exact failed axiom. `thm-finite-table-coloring-termination-and-correctness` proves the O(m^3) axiom checks and at most m^a assignments for a arcs, with exact extension bijections. Proofs are local finite derivations from the crossing convention; no unexamined fundamental-quandle classification theorem is imported.')
append_pair(10,'**Effective and simple-homotopy boundary:** Algorithmic inputs use a computable field with encoded exact arithmetic/equality (e.g. Q, a specified number field, or finite field), a finite presentation and explicit matrices. Extension is checked on finitely many relators; acyclicity and denominators by exact rational-function linear algebra. Unencoded arbitrary fields are theorem-only data. The Wada/torsion comparison binds the cellular presentation of a genuine exterior spine, its oriented lifted bases and simple expansions/collapses; arbitrary group presentations do not silently identify their presentation complexes with the exterior. The local Fox chain rule, the fundamental identity Σ_j ∂r/∂x_j (x_j−1)=r−1, and the torsion product formula are separately owned suppliers. Nonacyclic input returns zero torsion by the declared convention, not an undefined determinant division.')
append_pair(12,'**Necessary definition and invariance suppliers:** `def-seifert-s-equivalence-and-conway-normalization` defines integral unimodular basis congruence and elementary Seifert enlargements/reductions; it defines the Conway polynomial by ∇_unknot=1 and ∇_+−∇_−=z∇_0 with Δ_K(t)=∇_K(t^(1/2)−t^(−1/2)) after symmetric Δ(1)=1 normalization. `thm-seifert-s-equivalence-and-conway-arf-bridge` proves ambient-isotopic surfaces have S-equivalent forms by common stabilizations, then derives Arf(K)=a_2(∇_K) mod2 by a symplectic-basis determinant expansion. This explicitly discharges the previously unnamed Conway convention.')
